  (face): n, k, r, d in NN, Pr in Chamber(k, n), pi, rho in Point(k), R in IntForms(r, n), lambda, lambda2 in QQ>=0, r = d + 1, (forall j : exists yP, yM in Point(k) : (forall iota : pi_(iota) + rho_(iota) = 0 => yP_(iota) + yM_(iota) = 0), (forall x in Exponent(n) : x_(j) + (sum iota, yP_(iota) * (sum i, Pr.N_(iota)_(i) * x_(i))) + (sum iota, yM_(iota) * (sum i, Pr.P_(iota)_(i) * x_(i))) = (sum iota, yP_(iota) * (sum i, Pr.P_(iota)_(i) * x_(i))) + (sum iota, yM_(iota) * (sum i, Pr.N_(iota)_(i) * x_(i))))), (forall vP, vM in Point(n) : (forall iota : 0 < pi_(iota) => (sum i, Pr.P_(iota)_(i) * vP_(i)) + (sum i, Pr.N_(iota)_(i) * vM_(i)) = (sum i, Pr.N_(iota)_(i) * vP_(i)) + (sum i, Pr.P_(iota)_(i) * vM_(i))) => exists zP, zM in Point(r) : (sum l, zP_(l)) = (sum l, zM_(l)), (forall i : vP_(i) + (sum l, zM_(l) * R_(l)_(i)) = vM_(i) + (sum l, zP_(l) * R_(l)_(i)))), (forall zP, zM in Point(r) : (forall i : (sum l, zP_(l) * R_(l)_(i)) = sum l, zM_(l) * R_(l)_(i)), (sum l, zP_(l)) = (sum l, zM_(l)) => forall l : zP_(l) = zM_(l)) : exists g, O, K in NN : exists zeta in IntForms(n, k) : exists nuP, nuM in Forms(n, n) : exists A, B, h in Exponent(n) : exists psiP, psiM in Forms(r, n) : exists gP, gM in Point(r) : lambda <= lambda2 + g, (sum iota, pi_(iota) * Pr.op_(iota)) <= O, (forall alpha : A_(alpha) * (sum iota, pi_(iota) * Pr.op_(iota)) + B_(alpha) * (sum iota, rho_(iota) * Pr.op_(iota)) <= O), (forall alpha : forall iota : zeta_(alpha)_(iota) <= A_(alpha) * pi_(iota) + B_(alpha) * rho_(iota)), (forall i : forall x in Exponent(n) : x_(i) + (sum alpha, (nuP_(i)_(alpha) * (sum iota, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * (sum j, Pr.N_(iota)_(j) * x_(j))) + nuM_(i)_(alpha) * (sum iota, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * (sum j, Pr.P_(iota)_(j) * x_(j))))) = sum alpha, (nuP_(i)_(alpha) * (sum iota, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * (sum j, Pr.P_(iota)_(j) * x_(j))) + nuM_(i)_(alpha) * (sum iota, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * (sum j, Pr.N_(iota)_(j) * x_(j))))), 2^O * (prod alpha, (A_(alpha) + B_(alpha) + O + 1)) * (prod i in 1..n, i) * 2^(n + 1) <= K, (forall alpha : B_(alpha) * g <= B_(alpha) * g * h_(alpha)), (forall alpha : h_(alpha) <= 1), (sum alpha, h_(alpha)) <= d, (forall kk : forall z in Exponent(r) : (sum l, z_(l) * ((sum i, psiP_(kk)_(i) * R_(l)_(i)) + gP_(kk))) = (sum l, z_(l) * ((sum i, psiM_(kk)_(i) * R_(l)_(i)) + gM_(kk))) + z_(kk))
  origin: ?{\text{form proved, from the certificate with explicit constants; with a complete certificate, at the rows of a monomial ideal the two bounds give the order of its readout on dyadic cells, the case of equality of \cite[Theorem~1.3]{Lin2017}; for a chamber with no identities, the content}\ \mathbf 1\ \text{and the whole orthant, the order is the leading pole of the cone sums \cite[Theorem~4.2 with Remark~(1), Lemma~5.4]{DenefHoornaert2001} at}\ p=2\text{, and over the reals the same case of \cite[Theorem~1.3]{Lin2017}, which for a distance above one goes back to \cite[Theorem~0.4]{Varchenko1976}; (weak) cited; form proved: the easy half of the duality theorem of linear programming \cite[Corollary~7.1g]{Schrijver1986}, as a tie of positive forms; for a chamber with no identities and the content}\ \mathbf 1\ \text{it is the bound by the Newton distance \cite[Lemma~5.3]{DenefHoornaert2001}, the value its inverse; (above) and (below) form proved: the combination of each coordinate is a mixture of two price vectors of the content, whose ties with the content and the value are the equality case of weak duality (complementary slackness), and the points are optimal points of the chamber; (face) form proved, from \cref{fact:basis} and \cref{fact:dual}: a basis among the priced rows gives the combinations, its inverse the injection, and the coordinates of the points the dual basis; (core pivotsInject) and (core pivotsDirections), with (core pivotsRead) and (core pivotsReadRight): the inverse of a basis}\ D+R\ \text{from the inverse}\ \nu^D\ \text{of its pivots}\ D\ \text{is}\ (I+K)^{-1}\nu^D\ \text{with}\ K=\nu^DR\text{, given by the Neumann series}\ \sum_t(-1)^tK^t\nu^D\text{, finite when}\ K\ \text{is nilpotent \cite[Section~1]{Thomas2021}, and split into its even powers}\ \nu^P=\sum_{t\ \mathrm{even}}K^t\nu^D\ \text{and its odd powers}\ \nu^M=\sum_{t\ \mathrm{odd}}K^t\nu^D\text{; at}\ K^2=0\ \text{it is the Sherman--Morrison--Woodbury formula \cite[Section~1, formula~(1.1)]{Xu2017} at the capacitance}\ I+V^{*}A^{-1}U=I\text{, for a factorization}\ R=UV^{*}\ \text{of full rank, since then}\ K^2=0\ \text{exactly when}\ V^{*}\nu^DU=0\text{; form proved over}\ \Q_{\ge0}\text{: the inverse is the balance}\ (\nu^P,\nu^M)\text{, each of}\ B^{-1}B=I\ \text{and}\ BB^{-1}=I\ \text{a tie of positive sums, and the two recursions}\ \nu^P=\nu^D+\nu^MR\,\nu^D,\ \nu^M=\nu^PR\,\nu^D\ \text{and their mirror images}\ \nu^P=\nu^D+\nu^DR\,\nu^M,\ \nu^M=\nu^DR\,\nu^P\text{, both from}\ K^t\nu^D=\nu^D(R\nu^D)^t\text{, are hypotheses, so that no depth and no division beyond the pivots enters; (core least) form proved: the certificate of the least element of a system each of whose rows has at most one positive coefficient (a Horn system), whose feasible points are closed under the coordinatewise least \cite[Lemma~2.3]{KimuraSuzuki2019}, stated there for the integer points of a bounded box; over}\ \Q_{\ge0}\ \text{the existence of the least point needs the attainment of a linear program and is not stated: every feasible point is at least}\ \nu\ \text{times the need, by (weak) at the unit contents with the rows of the table}\ \nu\zeta\text{, of one sign by hypothesis, as prices; (core pivotsOneSign): for a basis with its pivots}\ D\ \text{on the side of}\ P\ \text{and its gains}\ R\ \text{on the side of}\ N\text{, the left inverse is the same series with no sign,}\ \sum_tK^t\nu^D\text{, the solution of}\ \nu=\nu^D+\nu R\,\nu^D\text{, a hypothesis; (core leastReadout): the inverse is not written: a point}\ \hat x\ \text{strict at every row of the one-sign system}\ \mathrm{diag}(d)\,y+b^+\ge Ry+b^-\ \text{gives a positive inverse by \cref{fact:mmatrix}, so every point of the system dominates the solution}\ x^*\ \text{of its tie, a readout of}\ 2n\ \text{numbers in place of the}\ n^2\ \text{entries of}\ \nu\text{, also on a cycle of gains of product below one, where the series does not end}}

-- (weak) multiplies each row by its price and sums. (above): weak duality at \(\pi\) puts the content
-- of a feasible point at least at \(\kappa\), up to the offset \(O\); sorted into shells by content, the masses halve
-- from one shell to the next, and the slacks of a basis of rows, priced by \(A\pi+B\rho\), inject each shell into a box
-- whose sides grow linearly in its index and in \(L\), so a geometric sum bounds the weighted count. (below) is (core
-- lower): the points \(u_0+\sum_lx_lR_l\) with \(\sum_lx_l=m\) are feasible, told apart by the barycentric coordinates
-- of the directions, inside the box and of content at most \(\kappa+K_0\), and there are \(\binom{m+d}{d}\ge L^d/D\) of
-- them. (face): \cref{fact:basis,fact:dual} give the data of (above) with at most \(d\) rows of the
-- basis outside those priced by \(\pi\), so the power of \(L\) in (above) is at most \(L^d\). (weak) is the easy half of
-- the duality theorem of linear programming \cite[Corollary~7.1g]{Schrijver1986}, as a tie of positive forms; for a
-- chamber with no identities and the content \(\mathbf 1\) it is the bound by the Newton distance
-- \cite[Lemma~5.3]{DenefHoornaert2001}, the value its inverse. With a complete certificate, at the rows of a monomial
-- ideal the two bounds give the order of its readout on dyadic cells, the case of equality of
-- \cite[Theorem~1.3]{Lin2017}, which for a distance above one goes back to \cite[Theorem~0.4]{Varchenko1976}; for a
-- chamber with no identities, the content \(\mathbf 1\) and the whole orthant, the order is the leading pole of the cone
-- sums \cite[Theorem~4.2 with Remark~(1), Lemma~5.4]{DenefHoornaert2001} at \(p=2\).
proof lem:count
  (weak) dual
  "core geometric" pascal
  "core scale" eq
  "core rationalScale" eq
  "core basisSum" chain[(sum i, c_(i) * (sum alpha, mu_(i)_(alpha) * (sum iota, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * X_(iota)_(j)))) = (sum i, (sum alpha, c_(i) * (mu_(i)_(alpha) * (sum iota, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * X_(iota)_(j))))) by eq; = (sum alpha, (sum i, c_(i) * (mu_(i)_(alpha) * (sum iota, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * X_(iota)_(j))))) by eq; = (sum alpha, (sum i, c_(i) * mu_(i)_(alpha) * (sum iota, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * X_(iota)_(j)))) by eq; = (sum alpha, (sum i, c_(i) * mu_(i)_(alpha)) * (sum iota, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * X_(iota)_(j))) by eq; = (sum alpha, (sum iota, (sum i, c_(i) * mu_(i)_(alpha)) * (zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * X_(iota)_(j)))) by eq; = (sum iota, (sum alpha, (sum i, c_(i) * mu_(i)_(alpha)) * (zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * X_(iota)_(j)))) by eq; = (sum iota, (sum alpha, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * (sum i, c_(i) * mu_(i)_(alpha)) * X_(iota)_(j))) by eq; = (sum iota, (sum alpha, zeta_(alpha)_(iota) * (sum i, c_(i) * mu_(i)_(alpha))) * X_(iota)_(j)) by eq; = (sum iota, pm_(iota) * X_(iota)_(j)) by eq]
